        "description": "",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the &#8216;/wp-content/plugins/pausepage&#8217; directory, or install it via the Plugins menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Go to <strong>Settings &gt;&gt; General</strong>, scroll to the bottom, and check &#8220;Enable Coming Soon &amp; Maintenance Mode&#8221;.</li>\n<li>Choose the page you want to use as your maintenance page.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='can%20i%20use%20a%20custom%20page%3F'>\nCan I use a custom page?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes! The AJAX-powered selector lets you choose any published page on your site.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='will%20admins%20still%20see%20the%20full%20site%3F'>\nWill admins still see the full site?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Logged-in administrators are never redirected and can continue working on the site.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='does%20this%20affect%20the%20wordpress%20login%20page%20or%20dashboard%3F'>\nDoes this affect the WordPress login page or dashboard?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. It only redirects the <strong>front-end</strong> for non-admin visitors.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": ""
    },
    "short_description": "Effortless Coming Soon and Maintenance Mode - redirect all visitors to a selected page while allowing admins full access.",
